# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

Manage a SQL view over existing data. Changes to the query update the view in
place. Moving or renaming it requires replacement.

## Writing the query

Supply the query body, not `CREATE VIEW ... AS`. Semicolons are rejected.
Use `templatefile` for longer SQL and pass resource names as template inputs.
When a SQL file refers to a table without referencing its Terraform resource,
add an explicit `depends_on` so the table exists first.

A view does not materialize results. For a share that must be self-contained,
consider a physical marts table rather than a view referencing unshared raw data.

## Lifecycle and import

Destroy removes the view, not its source tables. Import uses
`<database>.<schema>.<view>` and reads the canonical query body. Match the
imported SELECT body before applying changes.

See [warehouse modeling](../guides/warehouse-examples.md).

